---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/home.scss';
---

<Layout title="Ask Me About GitHub">
  <div class="topbar">
    <a href="https://github.com/petersonjdNIH" class="topbar-title">
      <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      petersonjdNIH
    </a>
    <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" aria-label="Toggle dark and light mode">
      <svg class="icon-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21.64 13a1 1 0 0 0-1.05-.14 8.05 8.05 0 0 1-3.37.73 8.15 8.15 0 0 1-8.14-8.1 8.59 8.59 0 0 1 .25-2A1 1 0 0 0 8 2.36a10.14 10.14 0 1 0 13.69 13.19 1 1 0 0 0-.05-2.55Z"/></svg>
      <svg class="icon-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V1a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2a1 1 0 0 1-1 1Zm0 19a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-2a1 1 0 0 1 2 0v2a1 1 0 0 1-1 1ZM4 13H2a1 1 0 0 1 0-2h2a1 1 0 0 1 0 2Zm19 0h-2a1 1 0 0 1 0-2h2a1 1 0 0 1 0 2ZM6.34 7.76a1 1 0 0 1-.71-.29L4.22 6.05a1 1 0 1 1 1.41-1.41L7.05 6.05a1 1 0 0 1-.71 1.71Zm12.02 12.02a1 1 0 0 1-.71-.29l-1.41-1.42a1 1 0 0 1 1.41-1.41l1.42 1.41a1 1 0 0 1-.71 1.71ZM5.63 19.78a1 1 0 0 1-.71-1.71l1.42-1.41a1 1 0 0 1 1.41 1.41l-1.41 1.42a1 1 0 0 1-.71.29Zm12.02-12.02a1 1 0 0 1-.71-1.71l1.41-1.42a1 1 0 1 1 1.41 1.41l-1.41 1.42a1 1 0 0 1-.7.3ZM12 18a6 6 0 1 1 6-6 6 6 0 0 1-6 6Z"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="header">
      <h1>
        Ask <a href="https://github.com/petersonjdNIH">Me</a> About GitHub
        <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="header-subtitle">Enterprise-scale GitHub consolidation, governance, and modern development practices... oh my!</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sections">
      <div class="section">
        <h2>GitHub Enterprise Consolidation</h2>
        <p>I led <span class="highlight">one of the largest federal code platform consolidations</span>, consolidating <a href="https://github.com/nihgov">NIH on GitHub.com</a> while maintaining security and compliance.</p>
        <p>I built that expertise in enterprise migration strategy, identity federation, and Zero Trust security implementation previously at <a href="https://github.com/nihgov">NIH</a>, and now apply it across <a href="https://github.com/ARPA-H">ARPA-H</a> and <a href="https://github.com/hhs">HHS</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>NIH GitHub Resource Center</h2>
        <p>I built <a href="https://github.nih.gov">github.nih.gov</a>, the resource center supporting the rollout of GitHub Enterprise Cloud across NIH's Institutes and Centers. It covers onboarding, licensing, and training under a simple mission: <span class="highlight">supporting the code that turns discovery into health</span>.</p>
        <p>The site demystifies Git and GitHub for research staff, with direct pathways to hands-on support and the broader NIH GitHub community.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>NIH GitHub Management Portal</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://github.com/nihgov/github-portal/">github-portal</a> is NIH's fork of Microsoft's open source management portal. It gives anyone in the organization visibility into GitHub activity across the enterprise: repository creation, membership changes, and usage metrics all in one place.</p>
        <p>The portal also maintains a ledger mapping GitHub usernames to organization accounts, handles self-service organization joining, and manages GitHub Enterprise Cloud licensing and compliance tooling at scale.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>Agentic Development</h2>
        <p>I'm currently designing and implementing <a href="https://github.com/ARPA-H">GitHub's agentic potential</a> at the federal level: GitHub Advanced Security, Codespaces, and Copilot governance with controlled MCP registries.</p>
        <p>We're building with AI while maintaining strict compliance controls, peer review, and stringent security practices.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h2>Modern GitOps Architecture</h2>
        <p>I have 28+ years of experience architecting <span class="highlight">complex technology as enjoyable products</span> across cloud service providers (AWS, Azure, GCP) and over three dozen SaaS platforms.</p>
        <p>That experience spans Zero Trust security, cloud-native standards, control plane architecture, and infrastructure modernization across government.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer>
    <a href="https://github.com/petersonjdNIH">
      <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      petersonjdNIH
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/ARPA-H">
      <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      ARPA-H
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/hhs">
      <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      HHS
    </a>
    <a href="https://github.com/nihgov">
      <span class="icon-octocat" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      NIHGOV
    </a>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const toggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
    const htmlElement = document.documentElement;

    toggle?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const next = htmlElement.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
      htmlElement.setAttribute('data-theme', next);
      localStorage.setItem('color-scheme', next);
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
